* [[Kwame Nkrumah]] (1909–1972) – started the [[Pan-Africanism|pan-African movement]], which liberated many [[State (polity)|states]] from European colonialism.
* [[Arthur Wharton]] (1865–1930) – the first black [[Professionalism in association football|professional footballer]] in the world.<ref>J. A. Mangan, ''The Cultural bond: sport, empire, society''</ref>
*[[Harriet Tubman]] (1822–1913) –  American [[Abolitionism in the United States|abolitionist]] and military leader, famous for conducting the [[Underground Railroad]], [[social activist]], [[Suffrage|suffragist]].<ref>{{Cite web|title=Harriet Tubman (c. March 1822 - March 10, 1913)|url=https://www.archives.gov/research/african-americans/individuals/harriet-tubman|website=National Archives|date=2022-03-22|access-date=2025-11-29|language=en}}</ref>

